WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.500
06:40 — Wake check-in. Still half-asleep in the dark kitchen, Bilal opens Today on his iPhone and marks how the night went — no streak banner, no red shame, just a quiet tick before the bus.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:17.000
07:05 — Medicine list. He scrolls the medicine list on the same phone and ticks morning meds while the kettle boils, then drops the phone in his pocket and locks the door.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:25.500
13:20 — Craving forecast. On warehouse break he borrows the shared iPad and opens the craving forecast — a hard window flagged for late afternoon, so he texts his sponsor a simple “watching it.”

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:34.000
18:45 — Journal on the laptop. At home he types three honest lines on his laptop while tea cools — private, on-device, nobody scoring the words.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:42.500
21:10 — SOS contacts. Before bed he opens SOS on the phone and confirms his brother and sponsor are still one tap away, names readable, no scavenger hunt through contacts.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:51.000
22:00 — Quiet close. Laptop stays on the desk with Today closed. He missed one tick at lunch; the app does not punish him for it.

